  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper establishes collage as a formal geographical research method, providing a structured framework for its design, implementation, and analysis. It details practical guidance on material selection, session design, and organizer-participant dynamics, while contrasting its effectiveness when applied to adults versus children and demonstrating its utility for researcher reflexivity.",
      "why": "It provides a concrete methodological guide for researchers seeking to use creative, hands-on practices to explore feminist geography, offering a structured way for participants to visualize alternative spatial futures and for researchers to examine their own positionality."
